     [38;5;246msession.js owns sessionStorage; login() signature unchanged and storage-free; submit handler wires them together.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: login writes to store
     [38;5;246mlogin() stores the identity itself. Callers cannot forget, at the cost of a hidden side effect and auth/storage [39m
